    "snippet": "Jul 8, 2026         Cannot Move Out of Borrowed Content (E0507). This error surfaces when you try to take ownership of data through a reference. A reference only grants temporary access; it does not transfer ownership.You know ownership is well‑designed when a one‑line method solves a whole class of errors: Option::take and its cousin std::mem::take (for non‑Option types implementing Default) are go‑to tools for moving out of mutable references without violating borrowing rules.   Summarize",
